/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate20_vp_diButylCarbonate -- the vapour pressure of diButylCarbonate, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 step 2).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  diButylCarbonate`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION, committed
  before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to ONE
  laboratory and held out on ANOTHER that shares no author with it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/acs.jced.6b00517         23 pts  383.16-478.18 K  Yang; Xu; Yang
      10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012        21 pts  287.1-329.1 K  Kozlova; Emel'yanenko; Georgieva; Verevkin et al.
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      (none)

  PARTITION (the C16 rule, declared): FIT = the study with the most points,
  doi 10.1021/acs.jced.6b00517 (23 pts, 383.16-478.18 K); HELD OUT =
  the next largest sharing no author with it, doi 10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012 (21 pts,
  287.1-329.1 K).

  BAND: maxAAD 5.3 % (declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 21 points (5.1 to 5.5 %, mean 5.264 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean).

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: the record's Tb 480.6 K lies OUTSIDE the measured span 287.1-478.18 K: the fitted Antoine's own normal boiling point (P = 101.325 kPa) must lie within 2 K of it, or the fit is NOT promoted (an extrapolation that misses the record's own boiling point).

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares both
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  (filled in by bin/choupo-curate after the run)
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  diButylCarbonate;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diButylCarbonate-vapourPressure-acs.jced.6b00517.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/acs.jced.6b00517"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/diButylCarbonate-vapourPressure-j.jct.2008.02.012.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2008.02.012"; }
                role      validation;
            }
        );

        acceptance
        {
            maxAAD  5.3 percent;
            origin  "declared before the fit by bin/choupo-curate vp (C281 step 2): the held-out study's own stated relative expanded uncertainty U95(P)/P, AVERAGED over its 21 points (5.1 to 5.5 %, mean 5.264 %), rounded UP to two significant figures -- a mean held against the held-out AAD, which is a mean";
        }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
